     /Pg 6005 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

6233 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This project began with a question about whether increasing technology in cars was genuinely improving the driving experience\056\n\nThrough research\054 user interviews\054 multiple design iterations and two rounds of testing\054 I realised that the problem was never technology itself\054 but how it is introduced and experienced by the driver\056\n\nThe phone\055first HMI explores an alternative approach by removing the need for a permanently integrated infotainment display while retaining the digital features drivers already use\056 It brings together personal technology\054 essential vehicle functions and a simplified interaction model\056\n\nThe feedback also made one thing clear\072 a screenless approach may not be ideal for everyone\056 Device compatibility\054 visibility\054 integration and personal preferences all influence the experience\056\n\nMy final takeaway is that the future of automotive HMI should not be defined by how much technology a car contains\054 but by how intelligently that technology serves the person behind the wheel\056\n\nThe goal is not to add more features or remove every screen\056 It is to make every interaction purposeful\054 intuitive and worthy of the driver\047s attention\056)
     /K [ 114 ]
     /P 6234 0 R
     /Pg 6005 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

6234 0 obj
  << /K [ 6233 0 R ]
     /P 6237 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 6005 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

